1
00:00:00,260 --> 00:00:03,720
The girl on the witness
stand is seventeen years old.

2
00:00:03,840 --> 00:00:06,216
It is December 2012,

3
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:08,236
a criminal court in Brooklyn,

4
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:11,500
and she is telling a jury
about years of abuse.

5
00:00:11,740 --> 00:00:14,236
Behind her, in the public benches,

6
00:00:14,320 --> 00:00:16,736
several men quietly lift their phones

7
00:00:16,820 --> 00:00:18,520
and take her photograph.

8
00:00:18,620 --> 00:00:19,756
Not for the court,

9
00:00:19,840 --> 00:00:21,096
for the neighborhood,

10
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:24,736
so her face can be carried
home and passed hand to hand,

11
00:00:24,820 --> 00:00:29,080
a mark against the girl who did the one
thing she was never supposed to do.

12
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:31,040
Court officers catch them.

13
00:00:31,140 --> 00:00:33,240
The men are arrested on the spot.

14
00:00:33,360 --> 00:00:35,100
Sit with what that takes.

15
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:37,616
In the middle of a trial about a child,

16
00:00:37,700 --> 00:00:41,280
the instinct of grown men
in that room is not to shield her.

17
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:45,620
It is to make sure everyone back
home knows exactly who she is.

18
00:00:46,020 --> 00:00:48,680
The community she comes from is Hasidic,

19
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:52,856
part of the wider ultra-Orthodox
world the sources call Haredi.

20
00:00:52,940 --> 00:00:56,240
Around a quarter of a million
of them live in New York City,

21
00:00:56,340 --> 00:00:59,540
most of them across a handful
of Brooklyn neighborhoods.

22
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:02,436
These are streets
with their own ambulance service,

23
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:04,515
their own volunteer patrols,

24
00:01:04,599 --> 00:01:05,856
their own courts,

25
00:01:05,940 --> 00:01:10,080
and by most ordinary measures some
of the lowest street crime in the city,

26
00:01:10,340 --> 00:01:12,896
which is precisely what hides the problem.

27
00:01:12,980 --> 00:01:14,456
In 2009,

28
00:01:14,540 --> 00:01:17,436
the Brooklyn District
Attorney set up a special unit

29
00:01:17,520 --> 00:01:20,740
just to handle sexual
abuse inside this community,

30
00:01:20,840 --> 00:01:24,240
and in time announced ninety-five arrests.

31
00:01:24,380 --> 00:01:27,236
Then The New York Times
went through the records

32
00:01:27,320 --> 00:01:31,160
and found the office had inflated
what the unit had actually done.

33
00:01:31,340 --> 00:01:34,660
Case after case had quietly collapsed.

34
00:01:34,800 --> 00:01:37,660
And the reason was nearly
always the same one:

35
00:01:37,840 --> 00:01:40,176
the victim or the victim’s parents

36
00:01:40,260 --> 00:01:41,516
had pulled back

37
00:01:41,600 --> 00:01:43,900
under pressure from their own community.

38
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:47,780
You carry a reflex you have
probably never once examined.

39
00:01:47,980 --> 00:01:49,876
Something happens to your child,

40
00:01:49,960 --> 00:01:53,640
and your hand is on the phone
before the thought has even finished.

41
00:01:53,840 --> 00:01:55,096
No permission,

42
00:01:55,180 --> 00:01:56,716
no calculation,

43
00:01:56,800 --> 00:01:59,320
no glance at what the neighbors will say.

44
00:01:59,520 --> 00:02:02,556
Now set that reflex against a single idea,

45
00:02:02,640 --> 00:02:04,676
pressed into a person from birth,

46
00:02:04,760 --> 00:02:07,496
that making that call is itself a sin,

47
00:02:07,580 --> 00:02:11,100
that the real danger in the room
is the phone in your hand,

48
00:02:11,240 --> 00:02:14,696
that lifting it could cost
your family everything it owns

49
00:02:14,780 --> 00:02:19,040
while the person who did the harm
stays exactly where they are.

50
00:02:19,440 --> 00:02:22,440
So how does calling
the police become the crime?

51
00:02:22,560 --> 00:02:25,436
And who told a community
of tens of thousands

52
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:29,380
that the way to deal with a predator
is to say nothing at all?

53
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:33,420
Reach for the obvious answer here
and you will miss the whole thing.

54
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:36,916
This is not a community
that secretly shrugs at abuse

55
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:39,602
or quietly decides it does not matter.

56
00:02:39,702 --> 00:02:43,218
Most people inside it are as
sickened by it as you are.

57
00:02:43,302 --> 00:02:46,422
What holds the silence
in place is not approval.

58
00:02:46,602 --> 00:02:47,818
It is a rule,

59
00:02:47,902 --> 00:02:51,718
old enough and heavy enough
to override almost everything around it,

60
00:02:51,802 --> 00:02:53,238
and it has a name:

61
00:02:53,322 --> 00:02:54,338
mesirah.

62
00:02:54,422 --> 00:02:56,258
The word means to hand over,

63
00:02:56,342 --> 00:02:58,778
and the person who does it is a moser,

64
00:02:58,862 --> 00:02:59,938
an informer.

65
00:03:00,022 --> 00:03:04,438
For most of Jewish history, this rule had
nothing to do with shielding criminals.

66
00:03:04,522 --> 00:03:06,518
It was about staying alive.

67
00:03:06,602 --> 00:03:08,438
For centuries across Europe,

68
00:03:08,522 --> 00:03:10,658
the authorities were not neutral.

69
00:03:10,742 --> 00:03:14,062
A Jew handed to a hostile
government could be robbed,

70
00:03:14,162 --> 00:03:15,978
jailed, tortured,

71
00:03:16,062 --> 00:03:17,138
or killed,

72
00:03:17,222 --> 00:03:19,922
and his whole community
dragged down with him.

73
00:03:20,062 --> 00:03:21,922
So the law set hard.

74
00:03:22,062 --> 00:03:25,362
You do not deliver a fellow
Jew to the outside power.

75
00:03:25,482 --> 00:03:27,998
In its oldest and harshest form,

76
00:03:28,082 --> 00:03:32,062
the informer was treated as
a mortal threat to everyone near him,

77
00:03:32,182 --> 00:03:36,302
placed in theory beside a man
running at you with a raised knife.

78
00:03:36,522 --> 00:03:39,742
That is the rule this
entire story turns on,

79
00:03:39,862 --> 00:03:42,502
and here is the collision
at the center of it.

80
00:03:42,622 --> 00:03:46,178
The rule was built for a world
where the state was the predator

81
00:03:46,262 --> 00:03:48,882
and the Jew it came for was innocent.

82
00:03:48,982 --> 00:03:52,018
It was never written for a case
where the outside authority is

83
00:03:52,102 --> 00:03:54,078
trying to protect a Jewish child,

84
00:03:54,162 --> 00:03:57,542
and the fellow Jew it would hand
over is the one who hurt her.

85
00:03:57,962 --> 00:04:02,138
You cannot feel the grip of that rule
until you take its history seriously,

86
00:04:02,222 --> 00:04:04,738
because the fear underneath it was real.

87
00:04:04,822 --> 00:04:06,418
For a thousand years,

88
00:04:06,502 --> 00:04:08,378
in country after country,

89
00:04:08,462 --> 00:04:12,842
Jewish communities learned that the knock
at the door was rarely help coming.

90
00:04:13,142 --> 00:04:17,878
Informers from inside their own ranks
really did sell neighbors to officials

91
00:04:17,962 --> 00:04:20,242
who would seize everything they had.

92
00:04:20,362 --> 00:04:24,482
Families were ruined on a single
word passed to the wrong clerk.

93
00:04:24,582 --> 00:04:26,098
Out of centuries of that,

94
00:04:26,182 --> 00:04:28,482
a community built something durable,

95
00:04:28,622 --> 00:04:32,578
a deep instinct to settle its own
quarrels behind its own walls,

96
00:04:32,662 --> 00:04:34,538
in its own rabbinical courts,

97
00:04:34,622 --> 00:04:37,838
and never to run
to the outside power for anything.

98
00:04:37,922 --> 00:04:41,018
For most of history,
that instinct was not paranoia.

99
00:04:41,102 --> 00:04:42,118
It was accurate,

100
00:04:42,202 --> 00:04:44,022
and it kept people breathing.

101
00:04:44,282 --> 00:04:48,158
And understand how seriously
the old law treated the informer,

102
00:04:48,242 --> 00:04:52,062
because it explains the weight
a person still feels today.

103
00:04:52,462 --> 00:04:54,098
In its classical form,

104
00:04:54,182 --> 00:04:58,138
a habitual moser was placed
in the same category as a rodeph,

105
00:04:58,222 --> 00:04:59,318
a pursuer,

106
00:04:59,402 --> 00:05:01,802
a man actively trying to kill you.

107
00:05:01,922 --> 00:05:02,818
In theory,

108
00:05:02,902 --> 00:05:07,542
the texts allowed that such an informer
could be stopped by almost any means,

109
00:05:07,662 --> 00:05:09,622
up to and including death.

110
00:05:09,902 --> 00:05:12,902
Nobody is carrying out
a sentence like that now.

111
00:05:13,162 --> 00:05:16,298
But a rule that once ranked
informing beside murder

112
00:05:16,382 --> 00:05:19,738
does not shrink to nothing just
because the calendar turned.

113
00:05:19,822 --> 00:05:23,342
It travels down the generations
as a feeling in the body,

114
00:05:23,442 --> 00:05:24,858
a bone certainty

115
00:05:24,942 --> 00:05:29,862
that handing a Jew to the outside world
is among the worst things a person can do.

116
00:05:30,082 --> 00:05:35,402
The trouble begins when a survival reflex
outlives the exact danger that forged it

117
00:05:35,502 --> 00:05:39,682
and keeps firing inside a world
that has quietly changed around it.

118
00:05:40,082 --> 00:05:43,638
And this is where the angry
version of the story breaks down

119
00:05:43,722 --> 00:05:47,218
because the religious authorities
themselves have largely ruled

120
00:05:47,302 --> 00:05:50,018
that the old prohibition
does not apply here.

121
00:05:50,102 --> 00:05:51,558
In two thousand eleven,

122
00:05:51,642 --> 00:05:55,138
a rabbinical court in the Chabad
community of Crown Heights

123
00:05:55,222 --> 00:05:56,702
stated it plainly.

124
00:05:56,962 --> 00:05:58,958
Where there is evidence of abuse,

125
00:05:59,042 --> 00:06:00,902
mesirah does not hold.

126
00:06:01,022 --> 00:06:03,002
Their wording left little room.

127
00:06:03,202 --> 00:06:06,782
One is forbidden to remain
silent in such a situation.

128
00:06:06,981 --> 00:06:10,182
The Rabbinical Council
of America said much the same,

129
00:06:10,282 --> 00:06:13,658
that anyone who learns of child
abuse is obligated to take it

130
00:06:13,742 --> 00:06:15,838
straight to the secular authorities

131
00:06:15,922 --> 00:06:19,738
because the law against informing
was simply never meant to cover it.

132
00:06:19,822 --> 00:06:21,998
On paper, in the text itself,

133
00:06:22,082 --> 00:06:24,322
the question was mostly answered.

134
00:06:24,522 --> 00:06:27,058
Reporting an abuser is not betrayal.

135
00:06:27,142 --> 00:06:29,262
The rule was never his shield.

136
00:06:29,442 --> 00:06:31,498
Some authorities went further still

137
00:06:31,582 --> 00:06:34,858
and turned the community's
own logic back on the problem.

138
00:06:34,942 --> 00:06:38,802
If an informer is condemned
because he is a danger to others,

139
00:06:38,902 --> 00:06:40,598
then what, they asked,

140
00:06:40,682 --> 00:06:46,202
is an abuser who will move on to harm
the next child and the one after that?

141
00:06:46,322 --> 00:06:47,978
He is the pursuer.

142
00:06:48,062 --> 00:06:49,642
He is the rodeph.

143
00:06:49,882 --> 00:06:52,478
By the community's own ancient reasoning,

144
00:06:52,562 --> 00:06:57,158
the person you are obligated to stop
is not the one who picks up the phone.

145
00:06:57,242 --> 00:06:59,238
It is the man he is calling about.

146
00:06:59,322 --> 00:07:00,918
In strict legal terms,

147
00:07:01,002 --> 00:07:04,622
the case for silence had
very little left to stand on.

148
00:07:04,882 --> 00:07:06,638
So if the law had settled it,

149
00:07:06,722 --> 00:07:08,502
why did the silence hold?

150
00:07:08,682 --> 00:07:11,482
Because a rule does
not live only on paper.

151
00:07:11,622 --> 00:07:15,878
It lives in what a community
quietly rewards and what it punishes.

152
00:07:15,962 --> 00:07:18,762
And there the machinery
kept right on turning.

153
00:07:18,942 --> 00:07:22,478
One of the largest Haredi
organizations in America,

154
00:07:22,562 --> 00:07:23,998
Agudath Israel,

155
00:07:24,082 --> 00:07:25,298
issued guidance

156
00:07:25,382 --> 00:07:30,338
that an observant Jew should not take
an abuse allegation to law enforcement

157
00:07:30,422 --> 00:07:35,638
without first consulting a rabbi to weigh
whether the suspicion was serious enough.

158
00:07:35,722 --> 00:07:37,538
Whatever the intention behind it,

159
00:07:37,622 --> 00:07:42,078
in practice that dropped a gatekeeper
between a frightened family and the police

160
00:07:42,162 --> 00:07:46,277
and handed enormous power
to whichever rabbi they happened to ask.

161
00:07:46,457 --> 00:07:49,997
And circling all of it was
the social weapon itself.

162
00:07:50,177 --> 00:07:51,537
The word moser,

163
00:07:51,677 --> 00:07:54,753
the posters that can brand
a person with it overnight.

164
00:07:54,837 --> 00:07:57,533
A clean ruling in a law book is one thing.

165
00:07:57,617 --> 00:08:00,293
The fear of your children
left unmarriageable,

166
00:08:00,377 --> 00:08:01,993
your shop boycotted,

167
00:08:02,077 --> 00:08:05,953
your family frozen out of the only
world you have ever belonged to

168
00:08:06,037 --> 00:08:07,997
is something else entirely.

169
00:08:08,277 --> 00:08:11,777
That fear does not sit down
and read legal opinions.

170
00:08:12,477 --> 00:08:14,713
To see how that punishment travels,

171
00:08:14,797 --> 00:08:17,073
you have to understand the posters.

172
00:08:17,157 --> 00:08:19,453
They are called Pashkevilin,

173
00:08:19,537 --> 00:08:22,653
broadsheets pasted
on walls and shop fronts,

174
00:08:22,737 --> 00:08:27,277
and for generations they have served
as the community's own front page.

175
00:08:27,437 --> 00:08:32,917
A name printed on one under the word
moser does not stay on the wall.

176
00:08:33,077 --> 00:08:35,253
It moves through the schools,
the synagogues,

177
00:08:35,337 --> 00:08:38,133
and the matchmakers until
everyone has heard it.

178
00:08:38,217 --> 00:08:40,693
And in a world where
marriages are arranged

179
00:08:40,777 --> 00:08:45,013
and a family's standing decides whether
its children can marry well at all,

180
00:08:45,097 --> 00:08:49,217
that one word can quietly
close every door a family has.

181
00:08:49,337 --> 00:08:51,357
Nobody needs to issue a threat.

182
00:08:51,497 --> 00:08:54,197
The threat is simply
understood by everyone.

183
00:08:54,357 --> 00:08:57,677
The gatekeeping does
its damage in a quieter way too.

184
00:08:57,857 --> 00:09:01,233
Tell a family to consult a rabbi
before going to the police,

185
00:09:01,317 --> 00:09:03,593
and you have built delay into the system.

186
00:09:03,677 --> 00:09:07,357
And delay is the one thing
a criminal case cannot survive.

187
00:09:07,497 --> 00:09:08,917
Evidence fades.

188
00:09:09,097 --> 00:09:10,633
A terrified child

189
00:09:10,717 --> 00:09:12,717
is talked gently out of it.

190
00:09:12,857 --> 00:09:16,373
Weeks drain away while
the matter is weighed internally.

191
00:09:16,457 --> 00:09:19,693
And by the time anyone looks
seriously at the authorities,

192
00:09:19,777 --> 00:09:21,573
the trail has gone cold

193
00:09:21,657 --> 00:09:23,937
and the will to act has gone with it.

194
00:09:24,217 --> 00:09:28,737
You do not have to forbid a report
to make sure it almost never happens.

195
00:09:28,977 --> 00:09:31,077
You only have to make it slow.

196
00:09:31,417 --> 00:09:34,053
Nothing shows the machine
running more clearly

197
00:09:34,137 --> 00:09:36,637
than the case in that Brooklyn courtroom.

198
00:09:37,037 --> 00:09:39,333
The accused was Nechemia Weberman,

199
00:09:39,417 --> 00:09:43,493
an unlicensed counselor in the Satmar
community of Williamsburg,

200
00:09:43,577 --> 00:09:45,433
a man with real standing,

201
00:09:45,517 --> 00:09:48,573
the kind of figure troubled
families were sent to.

202
00:09:48,657 --> 00:09:52,553
A girl who had been sent to him
by her own religious school said that

203
00:09:52,637 --> 00:09:54,273
beginning when she was twelve,

204
00:09:54,357 --> 00:09:57,293
across years of so-called
counseling sessions,

205
00:09:57,377 --> 00:09:58,753
he had abused her.

206
00:09:58,837 --> 00:10:02,473
And she did the thing almost no
one in her position ever does.

207
00:10:02,557 --> 00:10:04,317
She went to the authorities,

208
00:10:04,477 --> 00:10:07,437
and she sat in open court and testified.

209
00:10:07,617 --> 00:10:09,593
In December two thousand twelve,

210
00:10:09,677 --> 00:10:13,035
a jury convicted him
on all fifty-nine counts,

211
00:10:13,119 --> 00:10:16,395
and he was sentenced to a hundred
and three years in prison,

212
00:10:16,479 --> 00:10:18,419
later cut down on appeal.

213
00:10:18,579 --> 00:10:20,675
But the verdict is not the lesson.

214
00:10:20,759 --> 00:10:22,999
Look at what formed around the trial.

215
00:10:23,119 --> 00:10:26,875
A fundraising dinner was thrown in the
neighborhood to pay for his defense,

216
00:10:26,959 --> 00:10:29,059
drawing hundreds of supporters.

217
00:10:29,219 --> 00:10:32,415
One man was charged with trying
to buy the family off,

218
00:10:32,499 --> 00:10:36,195
reportedly dangling a sum
in the hundreds of thousands of dollars

219
00:10:36,279 --> 00:10:38,155
to make the whole thing vanish.

220
00:10:38,239 --> 00:10:39,595
Three brothers were charged

221
00:10:39,679 --> 00:10:42,675
after they tore the kosher
certificate off a restaurant

222
00:10:42,759 --> 00:10:45,175
run by the family of the girl's boyfriend,

223
00:10:45,259 --> 00:10:47,855
a deliberate strike
straight at their income.

224
00:10:47,939 --> 00:10:49,555
And those men in the gallery,

225
00:10:49,639 --> 00:10:52,175
arrested for photographing
her on the stand,

226
00:10:52,259 --> 00:10:54,799
wanted her face spread
through the community.

227
00:10:54,939 --> 00:10:56,295
She told the truth,

228
00:10:56,379 --> 00:10:59,715
and the reflex around her was
not to protect the child.

229
00:10:59,799 --> 00:11:01,699
It was to protect the man.

230
00:11:01,999 --> 00:11:03,955
For many who watched it unfold,

231
00:11:04,039 --> 00:11:06,574
the trial became a kind of watershed,

232
00:11:06,658 --> 00:11:09,755
the first time that whole
machinery of intimidation

233
00:11:09,839 --> 00:11:13,315
was dragged fully
into daylight and met, for once,

234
00:11:13,399 --> 00:11:15,515
with arrests and a conviction

235
00:11:15,599 --> 00:11:17,099
instead of a shrug.

236
00:11:17,639 --> 00:11:21,135
If you want the kind of story
that pushes past the outrage

237
00:11:21,219 --> 00:11:25,175
and actually shows you how a thing
like this holds itself together,

238
00:11:25,259 --> 00:11:27,335
this channel is worth following.

239
00:11:27,419 --> 00:11:29,539
It matters more than you would guess.

240
00:11:29,679 --> 00:11:32,575
And that is the part no
court can ever touch,

241
00:11:32,659 --> 00:11:36,639
because the real punishment was
never going to arrive through a court.

242
00:11:36,739 --> 00:11:37,915
It is social,

243
00:11:37,999 --> 00:11:39,415
and it is total.

244
00:11:39,499 --> 00:11:41,155
In a world this sealed,

245
00:11:41,239 --> 00:11:43,675
your whole life runs
through the community.

246
00:11:43,759 --> 00:11:44,795
Your school,

247
00:11:44,879 --> 00:11:45,875
your job,

248
00:11:45,959 --> 00:11:46,975
your marriage,

249
00:11:47,059 --> 00:11:48,075
your friends,

250
00:11:48,159 --> 00:11:49,759
the roof over your head,

251
00:11:49,919 --> 00:11:52,419
every piece of it rests on belonging.

252
00:11:52,659 --> 00:11:55,575
So the cost of being
named the one who informed

253
00:11:55,659 --> 00:11:58,419
is not a fine and a few cold stares.

254
00:11:58,579 --> 00:12:00,855
It is the loss of all of it at once.

255
00:12:00,939 --> 00:12:03,255
Your other children may never be matched.

256
00:12:03,339 --> 00:12:07,239
Your family may be pushed out
of the only life it knows how to live.

257
00:12:07,399 --> 00:12:08,635
Weighed against that,

258
00:12:08,719 --> 00:12:10,454
most people who have been hurt,

259
00:12:10,538 --> 00:12:12,255
or whose child has been hurt,

260
00:12:12,339 --> 00:12:14,975
run the sum in their heads and stay quiet.

261
00:12:15,059 --> 00:12:18,879
This is why the district
attorney's cases kept falling apart.

262
00:12:19,039 --> 00:12:21,355
Not because the crimes were invented,

263
00:12:21,439 --> 00:12:24,535
but because the price
of seeing one through to the end

264
00:12:24,619 --> 00:12:27,619
was more than almost
anyone could bear to pay.

265
00:12:27,859 --> 00:12:30,819
You can watch it
in the numbers that unit produced.

266
00:12:30,939 --> 00:12:33,795
Of the roughly 50 cases
that had actually closed,

267
00:12:33,879 --> 00:12:35,295
according to The Times,

268
00:12:35,379 --> 00:12:37,739
around a dozen were simply thrown out.

269
00:12:37,839 --> 00:12:40,535
Most of the rest ended
in quiet plea deals,

270
00:12:40,619 --> 00:12:43,221
and only a handful ever reached a jury.

271
00:12:43,341 --> 00:12:46,417
Nearly two dozen defendants
walked away with probation,

272
00:12:46,501 --> 00:12:47,717
a reduced charge,

273
00:12:47,801 --> 00:12:49,057
or nothing at all,

274
00:12:49,141 --> 00:12:53,557
often because the victim or the parents
stopped cooperating partway through.

275
00:12:53,641 --> 00:12:58,357
The reporters could only match 47
of the 95 arrests to public records

276
00:12:58,441 --> 00:13:01,517
to begin with, and more than
half of those seemed to have

277
00:13:01,601 --> 00:13:05,521
little to do with the special unit
the office was taking credit for.

278
00:13:05,781 --> 00:13:09,741
And this is the trap outsiders
consistently underestimate.

279
00:13:09,841 --> 00:13:12,297
When people picture refusing to cooperate,

280
00:13:12,381 --> 00:13:14,457
they imagine a hard conversation

281
00:13:14,541 --> 00:13:17,301
and some lasting awkwardness at synagogue.

282
00:13:17,401 --> 00:13:20,357
They do not picture a person
who speaks little English,

283
00:13:20,441 --> 00:13:23,037
who was given almost no secular schooling,

284
00:13:23,121 --> 00:13:26,037
who has no outside network of any kind.

285
00:13:26,121 --> 00:13:30,317
They do not picture that person being cut
loose from the only society they know how

286
00:13:30,401 --> 00:13:31,397
to live in.

287
00:13:31,481 --> 00:13:33,837
For someone raised wholly inside,

288
00:13:33,921 --> 00:13:36,577
leaving is not moving to another town.

289
00:13:36,661 --> 00:13:40,461
It is emigrating to a country whose
language they were never taught.

290
00:13:40,661 --> 00:13:41,637
Seen that way,

291
00:13:41,721 --> 00:13:43,861
the silence is not cowardice.

292
00:13:44,221 --> 00:13:46,757
It is the clear-eyed
arithmetic of a person

293
00:13:46,841 --> 00:13:50,281
who can see they have nowhere
else on earth to stand.

294
00:13:50,701 --> 00:13:54,361
And it was not only the community
that bent itself around this.

295
00:13:54,581 --> 00:13:57,141
The outside institutions did too.

296
00:13:57,441 --> 00:14:02,101
The same district attorney who ran
that abuse unit made a telling choice.

297
00:14:02,461 --> 00:14:04,337
For defendants from this community,

298
00:14:04,421 --> 00:14:06,437
including some who were convicted,

299
00:14:06,521 --> 00:14:08,937
his office would not release their names,

300
00:14:09,021 --> 00:14:13,081
a courtesy it did not offer other
defendants across the same city.

301
00:14:13,261 --> 00:14:17,337
The stated reason was that naming them
might expose their victims in so small

302
00:14:17,421 --> 00:14:18,421
a world.

303
00:14:18,601 --> 00:14:19,477
The effect,

304
00:14:19,561 --> 00:14:20,597
critics said,

305
00:14:20,681 --> 00:14:21,817
was a quieter,

306
00:14:21,901 --> 00:14:26,897
softer brand of justice for one
powerful and tightly organized group.

307
00:14:26,981 --> 00:14:31,281
When a community can move tens
of thousands of votes as a single block,

308
00:14:31,421 --> 00:14:36,141
even the people whose job is to hold
it to account begin to step carefully.

309
00:14:36,321 --> 00:14:39,820
The silence, then,
was not kept by the community alone.

310
00:14:39,940 --> 00:14:42,741
It was met halfway by the city around it.

311
00:14:43,061 --> 00:14:47,201
The reason the city treads
so softly is not really a mystery.

312
00:14:47,381 --> 00:14:51,217
These communities often vote
the way their leading rabbis direct,

313
00:14:51,301 --> 00:14:54,741
in numbers large enough
to decide a close local race.

314
00:14:54,901 --> 00:14:56,977
A candidate who wins an endorsement

315
00:14:57,061 --> 00:15:00,481
can gather a whole neighborhood's
ballots in a single stroke,

316
00:15:00,581 --> 00:15:05,282
and a candidate who crosses the wrong
rabbi can lose them just as fast.

317
00:15:05,422 --> 00:15:09,738
That turns a religious minority
into a genuine political heavyweight,

318
00:15:09,822 --> 00:15:13,778
and it quietly teaches every
ambitious official the same lesson.

319
00:15:13,862 --> 00:15:16,438
Whatever is happening behind those walls,

320
00:15:16,522 --> 00:15:18,398
it is safer for your career

321
00:15:18,482 --> 00:15:20,402
not to look too hard at it.

322
00:15:20,642 --> 00:15:24,598
It would be easy to stop there
on the machinery and the wreckage,

323
00:15:24,682 --> 00:15:27,562
but stopping there would
be its own dishonesty.

324
00:15:27,702 --> 00:15:30,518
This community is not one single mind,

325
00:15:30,602 --> 00:15:32,618
and it is not standing still.

326
00:15:32,702 --> 00:15:37,902
The very same years produced survivors
who went public at a brutal personal cost.

327
00:15:38,082 --> 00:15:40,358
Advocates and whole organizations

328
00:15:40,442 --> 00:15:44,802
built by people who had left
or who had stayed in order to fight.

329
00:15:45,082 --> 00:15:48,258
Rabbis who said out loud from the inside

330
00:15:48,342 --> 00:15:51,338
that shielding an abuser is
a desecration of everything

331
00:15:51,422 --> 00:15:53,798
the law is supposed to stand for.

332
00:15:53,882 --> 00:15:55,518
The clearest rulings

333
00:15:55,602 --> 00:15:57,958
that abuse must be reported

334
00:15:58,042 --> 00:16:00,238
came from religious authorities,

335
00:16:00,322 --> 00:16:03,142
not from outsiders forcing their hand.

336
00:16:03,242 --> 00:16:07,302
More people report today
than reported a decade ago.

337
00:16:07,502 --> 00:16:10,718
Organizations now exist
for those who leave,

338
00:16:10,802 --> 00:16:12,158
offering the tutoring,

339
00:16:12,242 --> 00:16:13,478
the job training,

340
00:16:13,562 --> 00:16:17,558
and the legal help that someone
raised entirely inside the system

341
00:16:17,642 --> 00:16:18,958
was never given.

342
00:16:19,042 --> 00:16:20,938
Survivors have written books,

343
00:16:21,022 --> 00:16:22,338
given testimony,

344
00:16:22,422 --> 00:16:25,318
and stood up under their own
names in a world that prizes

345
00:16:25,402 --> 00:16:27,902
anonymity above almost everything.

346
00:16:28,182 --> 00:16:30,598
None of this was handed down from the top.

347
00:16:30,682 --> 00:16:34,518
It was pulled into the open by people
who loved the community enough to refuse

348
00:16:34,602 --> 00:16:36,498
the silence it asked of them.

349
00:16:36,582 --> 00:16:41,282
And the fear sitting under all of it
deserves to be handled with some humility

350
00:16:41,382 --> 00:16:45,258
because the distrust of outside power
was earned across centuries of that

351
00:16:45,342 --> 00:16:47,582
power being genuinely lethal.

352
00:16:47,682 --> 00:16:50,638
None of that unmakes what
was done to that girl.

353
00:16:50,722 --> 00:16:54,318
All of it explains why the silence
was so much harder to break

354
00:16:54,402 --> 00:16:58,402
than a tidy tale of good people
and bad people could ever admit.

355
00:16:58,622 --> 00:17:02,178
And if you are tempted to file
this away as something exotic,

356
00:17:02,262 --> 00:17:06,838
something that only happens behind the
walls of one strange and distant world,

357
00:17:06,922 --> 00:17:09,058
look a great deal closer to home.

358
00:17:09,142 --> 00:17:12,858
A church that transfers a priest
instead of reporting him.

359
00:17:12,942 --> 00:17:14,198
A university

360
00:17:14,282 --> 00:17:16,842
that buries an assault to guard its name.

361
00:17:16,982 --> 00:17:20,522
A police department that closes
ranks around one of its own.

362
00:17:20,662 --> 00:17:23,418
A family that tells a child to never,

363
00:17:23,502 --> 00:17:25,742
ever speak of what an uncle did.

364
00:17:25,882 --> 00:17:28,158
Every closed institution on Earth

365
00:17:28,242 --> 00:17:30,978
builds some version of this exact rule.

366
00:17:31,062 --> 00:17:34,538
The unspoken understanding
that whoever exposes the harm

367
00:17:34,622 --> 00:17:37,017
will be treated as the one who caused it.

368
00:17:37,297 --> 00:17:41,897
What this community holds is only
the oldest and most honest form of it,

369
00:17:42,037 --> 00:17:45,293
a reflex with an actual name written down,

370
00:17:45,377 --> 00:17:47,217
fought over for centuries.

371
00:17:47,397 --> 00:17:50,433
The rest of us are running
the very same program.

372
00:17:50,517 --> 00:17:52,957
We just never bothered to give it a word.

373
00:17:53,137 --> 00:17:56,613
So before you pass sentence
on the parent who stayed quiet,

374
00:17:56,697 --> 00:17:59,593
climb inside the choice
they were really handed

375
00:17:59,677 --> 00:18:02,917
because this was never
truly about one community.

376
00:18:03,677 --> 00:18:07,333
It is about what truth costs
when the price of telling it

377
00:18:07,417 --> 00:18:09,317
is every person you have.

378
00:18:09,517 --> 00:18:11,617
Picture it without looking away.

379
00:18:12,017 --> 00:18:15,093
If speaking meant losing
all of it in one stroke,

380
00:18:15,177 --> 00:18:16,053
your family,

381
00:18:16,137 --> 00:18:17,053
your friends,

382
00:18:17,137 --> 00:18:18,157
your work,

383
00:18:18,377 --> 00:18:21,033
every face you have known
since you were small,

384
00:18:21,117 --> 00:18:22,233
are you certain,

385
00:18:22,317 --> 00:18:23,573
genuinely certain,

386
00:18:23,657 --> 00:18:25,597
that you would still make the call?

387
00:18:25,737 --> 00:18:28,113
Say it honestly down in the comments

388
00:18:28,197 --> 00:18:33,573
because almost no one stays certain once
they stop judging and start imagining it.

389
00:18:33,657 --> 00:18:35,493
And somewhere in your own life,

390
00:18:35,577 --> 00:18:37,173
in a job you protected,

391
00:18:37,257 --> 00:18:41,033
a family you covered
for, a team you stayed loyal to,

392
00:18:41,117 --> 00:18:43,037
you already know your answer.

393
00:18:43,137 --> 00:18:46,008
You have simply never been
forced to say it out loud

